cle.md). ...     npx -y @aimarket/warden@0.16.0 scan\n    </p>\n    <!-- /aicom-readme-badges -->\n    \n    <p align=\"center\">\n      <a href=\"https://warden.modelmarket.dev/\">\n        <img src=\"docs/screenshots/readme/hero-3d.png\" alt=\"WARDEN — 3D gate chain: tools/list through static-scan, threat-feed, origin, and pinning to a recorded verdict\" width=\"100%\" />\n      </a>\n    </p>\n    \n    \n    > 🌐 **English** · [Русский](README-ru.md) · [Español](README-es.md) · [Français](README-fr.md) · [中文](README-zh.md) · [Glossary](https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/docs/localization-glossary.md)\n    \n    > [WARDEN quality cycle: MOMUS → AI-Factory → SKOPOS → shared node agent → deployment](https://github.com/alexar76/momus/blob/main/docs/quality-cycle.md).\n    \n    <!-- warden-try -->\n    **Check every MCP server on your machine.** No account, no API key, no model. The only network traffic is to the servers in your config.\n    \n    ```bash\n    npx -y @aimarket/warden@0.16.0 scan\n    ```\n    \n    ```text\n    WARDEN scan 0.16.0 · ruleset 11 sha256-RDXs+TaQoehA… · block at high\n      read .mcp.json (claude-code, 3 servers)\n    \n      ✓ allow   notes       claude-code    1 tool · score 0.90\n      ✗ BLOCK   evil-notes  claude-code    1 tool · score 0.00 · TOOL_DEF_EXFIL(notes) TOOL_DEF_SECRET_REQUEST(notes) THREAT_SSH_KEY_READ(notes)\n      ! error   broken      claude-code    could not start: spawn /nonexistent/bin/server ENOENT\n    \n    3 servers: 1 allowed, 1 blocked, 1 not checked, 0 skipped.\n    Details: warden-mcp scan --json, or --markdown FILE. To review a changed server: warden-mcp scan --lock warden.lock.json --update-lock.\n    ```\n    \n    Against two other open-source scanners on the same servers: on the held-out half of MCPTox (an AAAI 2026 benchmark; WARDEN's rules were written from the other half) WARDEN blocks 171 of 218 poisoned tools, mcp-audit 25, mcp-shield 41; on 986 public servers it blocks 3, they block 33 and 343. [Method and every number](docs/scanner-comparison.md) · [scan guide](docs/scan.md).\n    no protection:\n    \n    1. **authenticity** — Ed25519 against the key you pinned in advance (`feedPublicKey`);\n    2. **freshness** — the *signed* timestamp must be inside `maxAgeMs` (24 h by default), so whoever\n       serves the URL cannot replay a months-old snapshot and silently erase every record added since.\n       A signature says who wrote a document, never when you were handed it;\n    3. **determinism** — RFC 8785 canonical bytes, so publisher and verifier agree regardless of JSON\n       key order.\n    \n    [MOMUS](https://github.com/alexar76/momus) is a reference publisher of this contract\n    (`/warden/threat-feed`) if you want something to point `load()` at.\n    \n    ## Also in the box\n    \n    - **`EgressGuard`** — an outbound allowlist to wrap any request a tool makes. A tool reaching a host\n      you never listed is the classic phone-home tell. `*.example.com` matches subdomains; an empty\n      allowlist blocks everything rather than allowing everything.\n    - **`isSensitiveTool` / `classifyTools`** — glob classification of tools that must require per-call\n      approval. Sensitive tools stay *advertised*; they just cannot run unattended.\n    - **`canonicalize` / `parseJsonStrict`** — a strict RFC 8785 (JCS) implementation, also exported as\n      `@aimarket/warden/jcs` so another implementation can be byte-checked against it. Integers only\n      beyond `MAX_SAFE_JSON_INTEGER`, refusal (not escaping) on lone surrogates, and a reason code on\n      every refusal.\n    \n    ## ERC-8004 identity\n    \n    WARDEN is ERC-8004 agent [`96684` on Base](https://8004scan.io/agents/base/96684), registered on\n    2026-10-01 in the canonical IdentityRegistry `0x8004A169…a432` and owned by the AIMarket operator\n    wallet `0x1218ff36…Ad0a`. Its [registration file](https://modelmarket.dev/.well-known/erc-8004/warden.json)\n    lists the web page, the npm package and the hosted `warden-scan` endpoint. Transactions and how to\n    check them: [ERC-8004 identities](https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/docs/erc-8004-identities.md).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLOGOS — Federation Analytics Engine (https://alexar76.github.io/logos/)\nciteturn37search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Read-only analytics over the AIMarket federation — measured settlement-volume projections, catalog pricing, rolling z-score anomaly detection, Metis-assisted insights, and a prompt-injection-guarded assistant.\n\n🟢 Live demo GitHub ↗ Documentation ↗ ... DeepSeek V4 Pro (default), Anthropic Claude, OpenAI, Ollama, LM Studio — same named presets as MOMUS.\nLOGOS\n\nHome Analytics NEXUS AI Assistant Consumption\n\n[Button: EN] [Button: RU] [Button: ES] [Button: FR] [Button: 中文]\n\nFederation intelligence / live\n\n# LOGOS\n\nOne node. Every insight.\nRead-only analytics over the AIMarket federation — measured settlement-volume projections, catalog pricing, rolling z-score anomaly detection, Metis-assisted insights, and a prompt-injection-guarded assistant.\n\n🟢 Live demo GitHub ↗ Documentation ↗\n\nPart of the AICOM ecosystem · monorepo · MIT\n\n16 ENDPOINTS LIVE TELEMETRY\n\nMETIS COUNCIL NL INSIGHT LAYER\n\nROLLING Z-SCORE ANOMALY METHOD\n\n## 🚀 Try it now\n\nlogos.modelmarket.dev is live. Ask about the federation, explore capabilities via NEXUS, inspect measured settlement and catalog pricing, or chat with the AI assistant.\n\n📊 Dashboard ↗ 🧿 NEXUS ↗ 🤖 AI Chat ↗\n\n### Capability Browser\n\nFull catalog of every capability across the federation — names, descriptions, prices, provider hubs. Drop-down selector with live refresh.\n\nOpen NEXUS ↗\n\n### Manual Invoke\n\nCraft JSON input, hit INVOKE, and see the result. Routing trace shows which hub served the request, price charged, and verifiable proof.\n\nTry it ↗\n\n## 🤖 AI Assistant\n\nChat with the LOGOS assistant. Full read-only access to the analytics store. Prompt-injection guarded. Multi-provider LLM support. Voice input.\n\n### Multi-Provider LLM\n\nDeepSeek V4 Pro (default), Anthropic Claude, OpenAI, Ollama, LM Studio — same named presets as MOMUS. Switch provider, model, base URL via env vars.\n\ndeepseek claude openai ollama\n\nGitHub ↗\n\n### Input Guard\n\nWarden-style deterministic prompt-injection filter — blocks prompt extraction, role-switching, token smuggling, and delimiter injection before reaching the LLM.\n\nprompt-injection deterministic\n\nOpen AI Chat ↗\n\n## 💰 Consumption Tracking\n\nMeasured 24-hour settlement volume, 30-day projection only when that measurement exists, catalog pricing by hub, and CSV export. Missing telemetry remains unavailable—not zero.\n\nLOGOS — the analytical brain of the AICOM open agent economy\n\nMIT · Python 3.11+ · FastAPI · React · Three.js · 80 tests · 16 API endpoints · 6 dashboard views--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHome - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki (https://github-wiki-see.page/m/alexar76/aicom/wiki)\nciteturn37search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; # Home - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki ... The wider AIMarket stack lives in sibling satellites: hub, protocol, desktop SKUs, plugins, widget, SDKs, oracles, GAIA/ATLAS, Metis, LOGOS, SKOPOS, MOMUS/Treasury, Signal Hunt, DIOSCURI/HELIOS/THEOROS, ACEX, mesh, and MCP servers.\nState and artifacts live on disk (`data/`), you bring your own LLM keys, and there is no per-seat cloud pricing.\n\nTypical wall-clock (DeepSeek, without long repair loops): marketing_landing ~20–25 min; full_software ~25–45 min for a simple brief, up to hours when gates iterate.\n\n## Quick start (self-hosted)\n    \n    `git clone https://github.com/alexar76/aicom.git\n    cd aicom && cp -n .env.example .env\n    docker compose up -d --build\n    # UI → http://localhost:9080/admin/login\n    `\n\nThere is no default admin password in the repo — see Security and `docs/security.md`.\n\nMore detail: Quick-Start · Quick-Start-Ecosystem (full fleet) · Deployment\n\n## Role in the AICOM ecosystem\n\nThe public factory repo (alexar76/aicom) ships AI-Factory (pipeline + storefront). The wider AIMarket stack lives in sibling satellites: hub, protocol, desktop SKUs, plugins, widget, SDKs, oracles, GAIA/ATLAS, Metis, LOGOS, SKOPOS, MOMUS/Treasury, Signal Hunt, DIOSCURI/HELIOS/THEOROS, ACEX, mesh, and MCP servers.\n\nThe factory produces shippable products and machine-readable capabilities; the hub indexes, routes, and settles them for desktop apps, widgets, and autonomous agents. Auto-Mesh Pipeline — a run can discover peer agents on the hub, pay via channel, invoke them, and ship a connected product.\n\nFull map: Ecosystem · Oracles · Metis · Logos · Signal-Hunt · `docs/ecosystem/knowledge-base.md`\n\nProduction split: Factory :9080 · Hub :9083 — `docs/production-modelmarket-dev.md`\n\nMCP for agents: aimarket-oracle-gateway (35 oracle tools) · aimarket-mcp (web fetch/search + Metis verify) · Glama\n\nMetis (cognition): metis.modelmarket.dev · Metis · LOGOS (analytics): logos.modelmarket.dev · Logos\n\n## Wiki map\n\nTopic  | Page\n--- | ---\nEcosystem knowledge base  | `knowledge-base.md`\nEcosystem & satellite repos  | Ecosystem\nVerifiable oracles  | Oracles\nMetis (cognition + verify)  | Metis · RU\nLOGOS (federation analytics)  | Logos\nSignal Hunt (investigation game)  | Signal-Hunt\nInstall and first product  | Quick-Start\nDeploy the full ecosystem  | Quick-Start-Ecosystem\nPlatform owner  | Owner-Guide\nPipeline, discovery, remediation  | Pipeline\nAdmin UI and roles  | Admin-Panel\nDocker / production  | Deployment\nPasswords, CSRF, sandbox  | Security\nREST API  | API-Integration\nAI Market (AI-to-AI)  | AI-Market-Protocol\nAgents and gates  | Agents\nFAQ  | FAQ\nArchitecture (Mermaid)  | Architecture\nIndex of all `docs/`  | Documentation-Index\nLanguages (EN / RU / ES policy)  | Languages\nPublic demo mode  | Public-Demo\n\nTranslations (repo only, not wiki): `docs/USER_GUIDE.ru.md` · `docs/USER_GUIDE.es.md` · `docs/USER_GUIDE.fr.md` · `docs/USER_GUIDE.zh.md` · see Languages\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/alexar76/histor/tree)\nciteturn37search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago;     > 💬 **[Issues](https://github.com/alexar76/histor/issues)** · **[Pull requests](https://github.com/alexar76/histor/pulls)** both welcome. ...     > [WARDEN quality cycle: MOMUS → AI-Factory → SKOPOS → shared node agent → deployment](../momus/docs/quality-cycle.md). ...     | [AIMarket Hub](https://modelmarket.dev) | lists `histor.check@v1` in the catalogue |\n\n## histor\n\n\nSecurityObservability\n\nby alexar76\n\nOverviewSchemaSourceRelated ServersDiscussionsAdmin\n\nPython\n\nRemote\n\n  * histor\n\n  * deploy\n\n  * docs\n\n  * .github\n\n  * histor\n\n  * sandbox\n\n  * scanner\n\n  * scripts\n\n  * tests\n\n\nREADME.md\n    \n    `<!-- aicom-mirror-notice -->\n    > **🔄 Synced from a monorepo — but with a live history.** `histor` mirrors the\n    > canonical AI-Factory monorepo. History here is append-only (no force-push).\n    > **Pull requests are welcome** — merged PRs are imported back into the monorepo\n    > and re-synced here, so your contribution becomes canonical.\n    > 💬 **[Issues](https://github.com/alexar76/histor/issues)** · **[Pull requests](https://github.com/alexar76/histor/pulls)** both welcome.\n    \n    # HISTOR\n    \n    <!-- aicom-readme-badges -->\n    <p align=\"center\">\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/histor/actions/workflows/ci.yml\"><img src=\"https://github.com/alexar76/histor/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg\" alt=\"CI\" /></a>\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/histor/actions/workflows/pages.yml\"><img src=\"https://github.com/alexar76/histor/actions/workflows/pages.yml/badge.svg\" alt=\"Pages\" /></a>\n      <a href=\"https://histor.modelmarket.dev/\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/website?url=https%3A%2F%2Fhistor.modelmarket.dev%2Fhealth&label=live&up_message=up&down_message=down\" alt=\"Live service\" /></a>\n      <a href=\"https://histor.modelmarket.dev/log\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/endpoint?url=https%3A%2F%2Fhistor.modelmarket.dev%2Fapi%2Fv1%2Fbadges%2Flog\" alt=\"Labels in the log (live)\" /></a>\n      <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/docs-EN%20RU%20ES%20FR%20ZH-9c70ff\" alt=\"Documentation in 5 languages\" />\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/histor/blob/main/LICENSE\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexar76/histor/refs/heads/main/docs/badges/license.svg\" alt=\"License: MIT\" /></a>\n    </p>\n    <!-- /aicom-readme-badges -->\n    \n    <p align=\"center\">\n      <strong>HISTOR</strong> (ἵστωρ, “the one who knows because they saw”) — a public transparency log of MCP tool definitions<br>\n      What every remote MCP endpoint in the official registry advertised · when it changed · signed, appended, auditable\n    </p>\n    \n    <p align=\"center\">\n      <a href=\"README.md\"><b>English</b></a> ·\n      <a href=\"README.ru.md\">Русский</a> ·\n      <a href=\"README.es.md\">Español</a> ·\n      <a href=\"README.fr.md\">Français</a> ·\n      <a href=\"README.zh.md\">中文</a>\n    </p>\n    \n    > [WARDEN quality cycle: MOMUS → AI-Factory → SKOPOS → shared node agent → deployment](../momus/docs/quality-cycle.md).\n    \n    **Live:** [histor.modelmarket.dev](https://histor.modelmarket.dev) ·\n    **Landing:** [alexar76.github.io/histor](https://alexar76.github.io/histor/) ·\n    **Capabilities:** `histor.check@v1` · `histor.server@v1` · `histor.changes@v1` ·\n    **Port:** `9490`\n    \n    ## The problem, in one paragraph\n    \n    An MCP server can pass your review with harmless tool descriptions and change them later —\n    a new sentence in a description is all a prompt injection needs, and your client will pass it\n    to the model without asking you again. MCP has no content addressing for tool definitions, the\n    official registry verifies namespaces rather than contents, and a scanner on your laptop sees\n    only what the server shows your laptop. HISTOR is the missing public memory: it records what\n    each server advertised, signs it, and tells anyone who asks whether what they received is what\n    | **HISTOR** | remembers what servers advertised, publicly |\n    | [THEMIS](https://github.com/alexar76/themis) | admits a capability at publish time on a Hub |\n    | [AIMarket Hub](https://modelmarket.dev) | lists `histor.check@v1` in the catalogue |\n    | [AWR](https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/tree/main/awr) | the signed document format every label uses |\n    \n    ## License\n    \n    MIT — see [LICENSE](LICENSE). Part of the [AIMarket ecosystem](https://ecosystem.modelmarket.dev/).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\naimarket-momus · PyPI (https://pypi.org/project/aimarket-momus/0.1.0/)\nciteturn37search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: last month;   * Live: momus.modelmarket.dev on the oracle host · PyPI: `aimarket-momus` ...   * GitHub access: fresh GHSA advisories (global + `alexar76/momus`, `alexar76/aicom`).\n## Self-learning + threat intelligence\n\nMOMUS gets better at finding bugs over time.\n    \n    flowchart LR\n      OWN[Own confirmed/refuted<br/>findings] --> POST\n      PEER[Peers' findings] --> POST\n      FEEDS[[CISA KEV · OSV ·<br/>GHSA global + own repos]] -- prompt-firewalled --> CARDS[Knowledge cards]\n      CARDS --> POST[(Beta posteriors per<br/>attack-class × target-kind)]\n      POST -- UCB1 ordering --> NEXT[Next scan probes<br/>the promising classes first]\n    \n\n  * A UCB1 bandit over `(attack-class, target-kind)` decides which probes run first. Own confirmed findings raise a class; refutations lower it; the outside world folds in as a Bayesian prior.\n  * GitHub access: fresh GHSA advisories (global + `alexar76/momus`, `alexar76/aicom`).\n  * Fetched reports are untrusted DATA, never instructions. They are scrubbed (NFKC, zero-width / bidi stripped), fenced with a per-call nonce + canary, classified into a fixed category set, and can only nudge probe weights/seeds — never add a target, change the gate, or authorize a payout. A report that trips the injection detector is flagged and downgraded to the deterministic classifier.\n\n* * *\n\n## LLMs — your choice\n\nSelectable via `MOMUS_LLM_PROVIDER`:\n\nname  | what  | default endpoint\n--- | --- | ---\n`deepseek`  | prod default — DeepSeek V4 Pro  | `api.deepseek.com/v1`\n`anthropic`  | Claude (native `/v1/messages`)  | `api.anthropic.com`\n`openai`  | any OpenAI-compatible API  | `api.openai.com/v1`\n`ollama`  | local Ollama  | `host.docker.internal:11434/v1`\n`lmstudio`  | local LM Studio  | `host.docker.internal:1234/v1`\n`metis`  | the ecosystem's own cognition (its `/v1/verify`)  | `metis:9100`\n`offline`  | deterministic, no network (default when unset)  | —\n\nThe LLM is an idea generator and triager only — it proposes adversarial inputs and classifies reports. Nothing it returns can authorize money; that lives behind the Treasury's key and code.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWARDEN — MCP Security Firewall Server 0.22.2 – LightNow (https://lightnow.ai/servers/io.github.alexar76/warden)\nciteturn37search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: last week; Image: io.github.alexar76/warden icon ... Transport: stdio (`npx -y @aimarket/warden` / `node dist/mcp-server.js`).\n\n# WARDEN — MCP Security Firewall\n\nImage: io.github.alexar76/warden icon\n\nWARDEN — MCP Security Firewall\n\nby Alexar76\n\nio.github.alexar76/warden\n\nVersion 0.22.2 · latest Released 2 days ago\n\n## Run this server\n\nSuggested command for version 0.22.2\n\nRunnable\n\n`npx @aimarket/[email protected]`\n\nConfigure & connect\n\n## About\n\nMCP security firewall: stdio wrap proxy or inspection tools; zero runtime dependencies.\n\nSource\n    ImageOfficial Registry\n\nCategory\n    Developer Tools\n\nTransport mode\n    Local\n\nProtocol version\n    \n\nMCP 2025-03-26\n\nCapabilities\n    \n\n9 0 0\n\nLicense\n    MIT\n\nGitHub\n    0 GitHub stars\n\nReleases\n    8 versions\n\nView repositoryMCP RegistryReport a problem\n\n# WARDEN — MCP security firewall\n\nVets what an MCP server says its tools do — tool poisoning, rug pulls, requests for secrets, instructions to send data elsewhere — against static rules, a signed threat feed, origin and tool-definition pinning, before any tool reaches the model. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\naquaveo/stable: simple list (including inherited indices) (https://public.aquapi.aquaveo.com/aquaveo/stable/%2Bsimple/)\nciteturn37search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; aimarket-momus\naimarket-hub\naimarket-logos\naimarket-mcp-packager\naimarket-momus\naimarket-oracle-core\naimarket-orchestrator\naimarket-personas\naimarket-platon\naimarket-provenance\naimarket-safety\naimarket-signal-hunt\naimarket-streaming\naimarket-tee\naimarket-treasury\naimarket-zk\naimaster\naimat\naimathkit\naimaths\naimcp\naimd-limiter\naimdl-coordinate-systems\naimdl-dashboard-api\naime\naime-detector-sdk\naime-xai\naimedicalcoding\naimee\naimelia\naimem\naimemory-client\naimepdf\naimepdftool\naimer\naimerlibrary\naimes-math\naimesh\naimet\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWARDEN — MCP Security Firewall - Odel Module Marketplace (https://odel.app/modules/alexar76/warden)\nciteturn37search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; @alexar76 MCP server · External ...     npx -y @aimarket/warden\n\nMarket/AI agent governance/WARDEN — MCP Security Firewall\n\nImage: WARDEN — MCP Security FirewallMCP server: One MCP server.\n\n# WARDEN — MCP Security Firewall\n\n@alexar76MCP server · External\n\nMCP security firewall: stdio wrap proxy or inspection tools; zero runtime dependencies.\n\nAI agent governancev0.16.0 MIT TypeScript\n\nFree no charge per call\n\nHow to install\n\nRuns on your machine from its package; the steps are below.\n\n  * Safety · AI5%Low risk\n  * Does · AIWritesCreates or changes data\n  * ConnectOn your machineRuns on your machine\n  * Popularity830 a weekUpdated 14 Oct 2026\n  * StatusAll clearChecked facts, not AI\n\nImage: WARDEN — 3D gate chain: tools/list through static-scan, threat-feed, origin, and pinning to a recorded verdict\n\nFrom the README\n\n## What it does\n\n  1. Reads\n  2. Writes\n  3. High impact\n\nAt most: creates or changes data: records, files, settings.\n\n## What it costs\n\nFree\n\nOdel charges nothing per call. The publisher may charge for its own service.\n\nRuns locally over stdio\n\nThis server isn't hosted — your MCP client launches it from a package registry. Use one of the commands below, or drop the config into your client (e.g. Claude Desktop).\n\nnpm@aimarket/warden v0.16.0\n\nRun\n    \n    npx -y @aimarket/warden\n\nMCP client config\n    \n    {\n      \"mcpServers\": {\n        \"warden-mcp-security-firewall\": {\n          \"command\": \"npx\",\n          \"args\": [\n            \"-y\",\n            \"@aimarket/warden\"\n          ]\n        }\n      }\n    }\n\nREADME 15 min read\n\n> 🔄 Synced from a monorepo — but with a live history. `warden` mirrors the canonical AI-Factory monorepo. History here is append-only (no force-push). Pull requests are welcome — merged PRs are imported back into the monorepo and re-synced here, so your contribution becomes canonical. 💬 Issues · Pull requests both welcome.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nroot/pypi: simple list (including inherited indices) (https://public.aquapi.aquaveo.com/root/pypi/%2Bsimple/)\nciteturn37search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; aimarket-momus\n-----------------------------------------------------------